class:: FeatureMedian
summary:: Trailing median of a control feature
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Median

description::
Sorts a fixed-size trailing window and returns its middle value, or the mean of the two middle values for an even window. A median suppresses isolated spikes without assuming a Gaussian distribution. All scratch memory is allocated at construction.

A negative trigger accepts every control block. A nonnegative trigger accepts only positive edges and holds the output between edges; this lets the caller align updates with analysis frames. frameTime must match that regular update spacing. Irregular triggers do not create a nonuniform regression. Nonfinite input is replaced by zero. Output stays zero until size accepted values exist. Cost is O(size*log(size)); storage is fixed. This independent order-statistic implementation applies the same basic median idea as vanilla Median, with explicit update triggers and a larger supported control-feature window.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Control-rate or scalar feature, with multichannel expansion for feature arrays.

argument:: size
Literal window size from 1 through 127, default 5.

argument:: trigger
Negative: update every control block. Otherwise update on positive edges.

argument:: frameTime
Seconds between accepted values. Zero uses the server control period; supply the actual period when triggering sparsely.

returns::
Median in the same units as the input.

examples::
FeatureMedian applies a sliding rank filter to reject transient anomalies and erratic pitch jitter from feature streams. In this example, it filters the pitch output from an acoustic saxophone solo: spurious octave jumps and unvoiced pitch glitches are stripped away, yielding a rock-solid pitch trajectory driving an expressive synthesizer lead. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: monitors the stabilized pitch contour.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, minFreq: 100, maxFreq: 1200, frameSize: 2048, hop: 0.25);
        var rawFreq = pitch[0];
        var medianFreq = FeatureMedian.kr(rawFreq, size: 7, trigger: -1, frameTime: 0.01);
        var leadSynth = Saw.ar([medianFreq.clip(40, 2000), (medianFreq * 1.005).clip(40, 2000)]).sum * 0.15 * pitch[1].lag(0.05);
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + leadSynth;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, medianFreq) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Median Filtered Pitch", ~mir2Bus, 100.0, 1000.0, "Hz");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

